{"id": "EUVD-2026-76353", "enisaUuid": "27240e4e-d21c-3ebc-8de3-60426b84cc15", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommufd: Avoid locking internal accesses during unmap\n\niommufd_access_notify_unmap() skips internal accesses because they do\nnot have an external unmap callback to invoke.\n\nHowever, the current test calls iommufd_lock_obj() before checking\nwhether the access is internal. If iommufd_lock_obj() succeeds, the loop\nthen sees the internal access and continues, bypassing the matching\niommufd_put_object() used by the normal unmap path. This leaks the\nobject reference taken by iommufd_lock_obj().\n\nCheck for internal accesses first so skipped entries are never locked.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/436189ee4bb2c7c993b945d68570dd38c3e4349e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50a66a63d1c841ae6b28a4551f642c1bba4c9529", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0dbcdf4473a614adbd732d567c9b39ac0e040e0c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89447", "GHSA-jq6v-47fj-pp2p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "33b66fbd-3d93-381d-8b4b-046765629faa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27b77ea5feaa8fcf385ea99ce757982b0ac9d1f0 <0dbcdf4473a614adbd732d567c9b39ac0e040e0c"}, {"id": "36c53b38-286c-3697-81b6-ea3902b8a627", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "68136ff1-a69b-327c-9f6b-4dc5e444d508", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27b77ea5feaa8fcf385ea99ce757982b0ac9d1f0 <436189ee4bb2c7c993b945d68570dd38c3e4349e"}, {"id": "7fe0bb7e-750b-3d5f-9b26-507df3a95186", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "adea227f-f304-30ab-a241-36029f1d1563", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "d04435d6-f473-31dd-a946-f324d666e2aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "f4d29d7a-56cc-37ca-aece-338712c22858", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "fe4aa210-50b9-3953-835e-5f1d34e0b785", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27b77ea5feaa8fcf385ea99ce757982b0ac9d1f0 <50a66a63d1c841ae6b28a4551f642c1bba4c9529"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2c30b595-3f09-3154-9469-de31d970586e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}